**Next Park visit:** first inspect the working tree and verify the running executable revision/profile and matching measurement artifacts; installation alone is insufficient. Verify the existing installed runner/comparison identity through P156/P155 as needed, then prioritize P153 → P70 → P67 → P36 → P66: frame/output attribution, actual graphics-consumer GPU/waits, complete CPU/GPU ownership, remaining wake causes and the ranked bottleneck report. Reuse existing instrumentation; absent signals are unavailable, not zero. Save source-stamped evidence, coverage gaps and overhead/loss observations. Then evaluate save/backlog, populated reveal, mixed input/glyph/layout, quiet settling and both-output/Firefox acceptance. Further speculative optimization and broad deferred tooling do not precede these measurements.

Completed measurement coverage, real system attribution, mixed-route repair, local-edit attribution, retained panels, surface fingerprint lookup and obsolete duplicate-ELF work remain retired as coding tasks. The previous sync/history/Karma delegation is historical, not a current ownership grant. Source-only implementations are not reintroduced into the coding queue; historical evidence and stable Record IDs remain.

**No blanket completion claim:** the current inventory has no additional specifically selected waste-removal implementation beyond the recorded batch. It still has conditional candidates, unfinished tooling and unclosed coverage. Do not interpret this as proof that all unnecessary computation is gone, or keep adding speculative caches while the owner is reviewing the candidate.

